  "scope_notes": {
    "Douady": "The paper supplies the Cech identification with H1(T_X) and the nonzero Kodaira-Spencer parameter. Douady supplies the finite-dimensional versal germ and its tangent universality. Smoothness of the receiving one-dimensional germ follows from its displayed injective substitution argument; no general unobstructedness is attributed to Douady. Metadata independently opened at the Numdam primary landing page: Ann. Sci. ENS(4)7(4)(1974),569–602, DOI10.24033/asens.1280.",
    "Stein": "Theorem9.18 is a congruence theorem. For an integral-coefficient difference, apply it at every prime ideal: each coefficient belongs to every prime ideal and hence is zero. This exact characteristic-zero passage must remain in the receiving application; the source is not described as directly stating that passage.",
    "Waldschmidt": "This current-run receipt covers exactly the two named rendered pages, not the whole paper or Bertrand1982 proof."
